# Server functions and auth

## The two-file pattern

- `src/lib/<feature>.functions.ts`: `createServerFn()` RPCs callable from the client. These validate input with zod, attach auth via middleware, and contain no secrets.
- `src/lib/<feature>.server.ts`: server-only modules that hold secret-bearing clients (Stripe, AI providers, web-push, Whoop/Oura). Only imported dynamically from `*.functions.ts` or API routes, never from client components.

Keep new server code in this shape. Do not put `process.env.<SECRET>` reads in `*.functions.ts` or any client-reachable module.

## Auth requirements

- Every protected server function uses the Supabase auth middleware (`src/integrations/supabase/auth-middleware.ts`), which validates the Bearer JWT and exposes `{ supabase, userId }`. The client side attaches tokens via `src/integrations/supabase/auth-attacher.ts`, wired globally in `src/start.ts`.
- Every protected API route under `src/routes/api/` verifies auth explicitly. Public endpoints live under `src/routes/api/public/` and must validate their own secret (`CRON_SECRET` for cron, Stripe signature for webhooks, HMAC for email hooks).
- Admin-only functions check the role through `src/lib/use-is-admin.ts` server equivalents, not client-side flags alone.

## Multi-user data scoping

- All queries scope by the authenticated `userId`. Caregiver reads/writes go through care scopes (`src/lib/care.scopes.ts`) and the `care_relationships` tables.
- Write operations on shared or sensitive data log an audit entry after success (`care_audit_log`, `phi_access_log`, `platform_rule_audit` are the existing patterns).
- Unauthorized cross-user access returns 404, never 403.

## SQL

- Migrations live in `supabase/migrations/`. Any dynamic SQL uses parameterized queries or tagged templates, never string concatenation.
- New tables ship with RLS enabled and policies in the same migration file.
- Sensitive token columns (care invite tokens, etc.) must not be client-readable. Use SECURITY DEFINER RPCs with `SET search_path = public`, `auth.uid()` checks, and REVOKE on the column. Pattern: `accept_care_invite()` in `20260613010000_security_hardening.sql`.

## Wearable sync timestamps

- Read and display `last_sync_at` for sync freshness. Do not use `updated_at` as a fallback (token refresh updates it without importing data).
- Server writes must set `last_sync_at` only when data was imported; empty webhooks/pings must not advance it.

## Email

- Transactional email goes through the queue: `src/lib/email/send.ts` (HTTP, user-context) or `src/lib/email/render-and-enqueue.server.ts` (cron, service-role). Templates are React Email components in `src/lib/email-templates/`. Always check `suppressed_emails` before sending.
